        [
            'table' => 'public_products',
            'slug' => 'hicon-pulper',
            'url_path' => '/product/hicon-pulper/',
            'title' => 'High-Consistency Pulper',
            'summary' => 'High-efficiency batch pulping system operating at 15–18% consistency for gentle fiber defibering, effective ink detachment, and complete contaminant retention during stock preparation.',
            'content_html' => '<h1>High-Consistency (HICON) Batch Pulper</h1><p class="product-description">The High-Consistency (HICON) Batch Pulper is engineered for advanced stock preparation lines processing waste paper (OCC, MOW, SOP), virgin pulp, and deinking grades. By slushing pulp at high consistencies of 15% to 18%, the system uses intense fiber-to-fiber friction to achieve complete fiber separation while drastically reducing specific power and water consumption per ton of pulp.</p><h2>Operating Principle & Technological Advantage</h2><p>Unlike traditional low-consistency pulpers that rely on mechanical impact, the HICON pulper features a specialized cast stainless steel helical rotor with contoured flights. As the rotor turns in the custom vat, stock is drawn downwards along the rotor axis and forced radially outwards, creating a high-shear vortex. Fiber bundles, flakes, and ink coatings are separated through hydraulic friction without cutting or shortening individual fibers. Heavy plastics, wet-strength film, aluminum foil, and wire remain intact in large pieces, preventing break-up into micro-contaminants that are difficult to isolate downstream.</p><h2>Key Features and Benefits</h2><ul><li><strong>15–18% High-Consistency Operation:</strong> Maximizes fiber-to-fiber friction to achieve rapid defibering with minimal specific energy input.</li><li><strong>Contaminant Preservation:</strong> Keeps non-fibrous contaminants intact for effortless removal in downstream coarse screening.</li><li><strong>Cast Stainless Helical Rotor:</strong> Precision-cast SS-304/316 rotor with hard-faced leading edges ensures extended service life and smooth vortex circulation.</li><li><strong>Enhanced Deinking Efficiency:</strong> Effective detachment of inks, pigments, and synthetic binders in graphic, writing, and tissue stock preparation.</li><li><strong>Robust Fabricated Vat:</strong> Corrosion-resistant stainless steel lining backed by heavy structural steel stiffeners for low-vibration continuous operation.</li><li><strong>Flexible Drive Configurations:</strong> Direct-coupled planetary gearbox or heavy-duty V-belt drive systems tailored to plant layout requirements.</li><li><strong>Automated Batch Control:</strong> Automated sequence management for recipe water addition, batch pulping, dilution, and bottom valve discharge.</li></ul><h2>Applications</h2><ul><li>Deinking and bleaching stock preparation lines for writing, printing, and tissue papers.</li><li>High-capacity recycled packaging paper production (OCC, Kraft linerboard, fluting medium).</li><li>Virgin pulp slushing and fiberization for duplex board and specialty paper grades.</li><li>Processing difficult wet-strength papers using thermal heating and auxiliary chemical dosing.</li></ul><h2>Materials of Construction</h2><ul><li><strong>Vat Body:</strong> Solid SS-304 / SS-316 clad stainless steel shell with external carbon steel structural framing.</li><li><strong>Rotor Flighting:</strong> Heavy cast SS-304 / SS-316 stainless steel with Stellite / Tungsten Carbide hard-faced edges.</li><li><strong>Extraction Chamber & Plate:</strong> Stainless steel 316L precision-drilled extraction plate with hard coating.</li><li><strong>Shaft & Bearings:</strong> Forged alloy steel drive shaft mounted on heavy-duty spherical roller bearings in sealed oil bath.</li></ul><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><ul><li>Operating Consistency Range: 15% to 18%</li><li>Throughput Capacity: 25 TPD to 650 TPD (Tons Per Day)</li><li>Vat Volumetric Capacity: 5 m³ to 45 m³</li><li>Drive Motor Rating: 90 kW to 750 kW</li><li>Operating Temperature Limit: Up to 85°C for heat-assisted deinking cycles</li><li>Discharge Consistency: Diluted to 3.5%–4.5% prior to coarse screening stage</li></ul>',
            'key_features_json' => '["15–18% High-Consistency Operation for rapid defibering with low specific energy input", "Contaminant Preservation keeping plastics, wet-strength films, and foils intact", "Cast Stainless Helical Rotor with hard-faced leading edges for optimal vortex circulation", "Superior Deinking Efficiency for detached ink removal in writing, printing, and tissue lines", "Robust SS-304/316 Fabricated Vat with heavy structural stiffeners", "Flexible Planetary Gearbox or V-Belt Drive options to suit mill footprint", "Fully Automated Batch Control for water addition, pulping time, dilution, and discharge"]',
            'applications_json' => '["Deinking and bleaching stock preparation for writing, printing, and tissue paper", "Recycled packaging paper lines (OCC, Kraft linerboard, fluting medium)", "Virgin pulp fiberization for duplex board and folding boxboard", "Processing wet-strength papers with thermal and chemical assistance"]',
            'materials_json' => '["SS-304 / SS-316 Clad Stainless Steel Vat", "Cast SS-304 / SS-316 Helical Rotor with Stellite/Carbide hard-facing", "SS-316L Extraction Plate", "Forged Alloy Steel Shaft with Spherical Roller Bearings"]',
            'technical_specs_json' => '["Operating Consistency: 15% – 18%", "Throughput Capacity: 25 TPD – 650 TPD", "Vat Volumetric Capacity: 5 m³ – 45 m³", "Drive Power: 90 kW – 750 kW", "Max Operating Temp: Up to 85°C", "Discharge Consistency: 3.5% – 4.5%"]',
