        [
            'table' => 'public_products',
            'slug' => 'disc-refiner',
            'url_path' => '/product/disc-refiner/',
            'title' => 'Double Disc Refiner',
            'summary' => 'Precision Double Disc (Twin Disc) Stock Refining System engineered for controlled fiber cutting, fibrillation, and freeness development across stock preparation and approach flow lines.',
            'content_html' => '<h1>Double Disc Refiner System</h1><p class="product-description">The Double Disc Refiner (Twin Disc Refiner) is a premier mechanical treatment solution for papermaking fibers. Featuring dual refining zones and floating rotor technology, it delivers controlled fiber cutting, external fibrillation, and swelling to enhance paper strength properties, sheet formation, and surface smoothness while minimizing energy consumption.</p><h2>Operating Principle & Mechanical Design</h2><p>Pulp slurry enters the refiner axially under positive pressure (1.5 to 2.5 bar) through twin stock inlet ports and is distributed symmetrically between two refining zones formed by fixed stator plates and a central floating rotor disc. Equipped with precision splined shaft technology, the lightweight rotor automatically self-centers between the refining heads under hydraulic stock forces. This eliminates axial thrust loads on motor bearings, guarantees uniform grinding gaps across both faces, and prevents uneven plate wear.</p><h2>Key Features and Benefits</h2><ul><li><strong>Floating Splined Rotor Shaft:</strong> Automatically balances refining stock pressure across both faces, eliminating axial thrust bearings and uneven plate wear.</li><li><strong>Ultra-Light Open Rotor Design:</strong> Lightweight rotor reduces rotating inertia by 60%, lowering no-load power consumption by up to 25%.</li><li><strong>Micron-Level Gap Positioning:</strong> High-precision electromechanical stepper motor or hydraulic positioner with continuous digital gap readout (accuracy ±0.01 mm).</li><li><strong>Tailored Refining Intensity:</strong> Customized CNC-milled refiner segment profiles designed for specific fiber types (virgin softwood/hardwood, non-wood, OCC, deinked fiber).</li><li><strong>Convenient Maintenance Door:</strong> Heavy hinged front door opens fully for quick, safe refiner plate segment changes and internal cleaning.</li><li><strong>Symmetrical Stock Hydraulics:</strong> Dual stock inlets ensure uniform flow velocity and balanced pressure distribution.</li><li><strong>Automation Ready:</strong> Seamlessly integrates with DCS/PLC systems for constant Specific Edge Load (SEL), specific energy refining, or freeness control.</li></ul><h2>Applications</h2><ul><li>Stock preparation for Kraft linerboard, testliner, corrugating medium, and duplex packaging board.</li><li>Refining virgin hardwood/softwood kraft pulp, bamboo pulp, bagasse, and bleached eucalyptus.</li><li>Post-refining and fibrillation of recycled OCC and deinked pulp for tissue and printing papers.</li><li>Approach flow tickler refining immediately prior to headbox for real-time freeness adjustment.</li></ul><h2>Materials of Construction</h2><ul><li><strong>Refiner Casing & Hinged Door:</strong> Solid SS-304 / SS-316 stainless steel wetted surfaces with cast iron structural housing.</li><li><strong>Splined Rotor & Shaft:</strong> Forged alloy steel main shaft with stainless steel sleeve and high-strength splined rotor hub.</li><li><strong>Refiner Segment Plates:</strong> SS-316L, 17-4 PH Stainless Steel, or Martensitic Chrome Alloys engineered for high corrosion and wear resistance.</li><li><strong>Shaft Sealing:</strong> Dual mechanical face seals or water-flushed braided packing glands.</li></ul><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><ul><li>Refiner Disc Diameter Sizes: 13", 17", 21", 24", 26", 28", 30", 34", 38", 42", 46"</li><li>Processing Capacity Range: 15 TPD to 500+ TPD per machine unit</li><li>Drive Motor Power: 37 kW to 1,200 kW</li><li>Operating Consistency: 3.0% to 5.5%</li><li>Operating Stock Pressure: 1.5 bar to 3.5 bar</li><li>Plate Gap Adjustment Precision: ±0.01 mm (10 microns)</li></ul>',
            'key_features_json' => '["Self-Centering Floating Splined Shaft balancing hydraulic forces across dual refining zones", "Ultra-Lightweight Open Rotor reducing no-load power consumption by up to 25%", "Precision Electromechanical or Hydraulic Gap Positioning with micron-level readout", "Tailored CNC-Milled Segment Profiles for specific fiber cutting or fibrillation", "Hinged Front Access Door for rapid refiner plate changes and maintenance", "Symmetrical Twin Stock Inlets providing uniform pressure and zero axial thrust", "DCS/PLC Automation for constant Specific Edge Load (SEL) and energy control"]',
            'applications_json' => '["Stock preparation for Kraft linerboard, fluting medium, and duplex board", "Refining virgin softwood/hardwood kraft pulp, bagasse, and bamboo pulp", "Post-refining recycled OCC stock and deinked fibers for tissue and printing grades", "Approach flow tickler refining for real-time headbox freeness control"]',
