            'title' => 'Screening & Cleaning System',
            'summary' => 'Multi-stage pressure screens and high/low-density cleaners engineered for complete contaminant isolation, shive removal, and stock purification.',
            'content_html' => '<h1>Pulp Screening & Cleaning System</h1><p class="product-description">The Pulp Screening & Cleaning System provides comprehensive stock purification across coarse screening, fine slotted screening, high-density cleaning, and multi-stage hydrocyclone plants. Engineered to protect high-speed paper machines from debris, shives, stickies, and abrasive grit, the system ensures optimal fiber yield and web runnability.</p><h2>Integrated System Components & Flow Dynamics</h2><p>Stock cleaning is achieved through sequential density-based and size-based separation stages:</p><ul><li><strong>High-Density Cleaners (HDC):</strong> Heavy-duty hydrocyclones operating at 2.5% to 5.0% consistency to centrifugal-force trap tramp metal, stones, glass, and heavy sand before coarse screens.</li><li><strong>Coarse Pressure Screens:</strong> Inward-flow or outward-flow screens with perforated baskets (1.2 mm to 2.5 mm holes) for isolating unpulped fiber flakes, plastic films, and large debris.</li><li><strong>Fine Pressure Screens:</strong> High-efficiency slotted pressure screens utilizing precision wedge-wire baskets (0.10 mm to 0.25 mm slot widths) paired with non-pulsating aerofoil rotors to eliminate micro-stickies, shives, and fine latex.</li><li><strong>Low-Density Cleaner (LDC) Banks:</strong> Multi-stage, low-consistency (0.5% to 1.2%) hydrocyclones equipped with ceramic lower cones for removing fine sand, bark, and light contaminants.</li><li><strong>Reject Sorters & Tailing Screens:</strong> Enclosed secondary and tertiary reject handling screens designed for zero-fiber-loss operation.</li></ul><h2>Key Features and Benefits</h2><ul><li><strong>Superior Contaminant Separation:</strong> High removal efficiency for micro-stickies, plastics, shives, sand, and bark while preserving usable paper fibers.</li><li><strong>Non-Blinding Aerofoil Rotors:</strong> Advanced rotor geometry generates high-frequency negative suction pulses to keep basket apertures continuously clear without hydraulic surging.</li><li><strong>Precision Wedge-Wire Baskets:</strong> Smooth-surfaced, mechanically interlocked or welding-free slotted baskets with Hard Chrome Plating (100–150 microns).</li><li><strong>Low Specific Power Consumption:</strong> Optimized internal fluid mechanics minimize differential pressure drop across all screen and cleaner stages.</li><li><strong>Abrasion-Resistant Hydrocyclones:</strong> High-purity alumina ceramic or polyurethane lower cone liners extend component life under heavy sand load.</li><li><strong>Zero-Fiber-Loss Reject Systems:</strong> Multi-stage cascade arrangements recover trapped fibers from reject streams before final disposal.</li></ul><h2>Applications</h2><ul><li>Coarse and fine stock screening in recycled pulp lines (OCC, MWP, MOW, SOP).</li><li>Approach flow screening directly upstream of paper machine headboxes.</li><li>Deinking plant screening and light-contaminant hydrocyclone cleaning.</li><li>Brownstock screening and knot removal in chemical pulp mills.</li></ul><h2>Materials of Construction</h2><ul><li><strong>Screen Vessel Body:</strong> SS-304 / SS-316L stainless steel, interior polished to mirror surface.</li><li><strong>Screen Basket:</strong> SS-316L wedge-wire welded or mechanical interlocked profile wire with Hard Chrome coating.</li><li><strong>Screen Rotor Assembly:</strong> Cast SS-316 with Stellite / Tungsten Carbide hard-faced aerofoil foils.</li><li><strong>Hydrocyclone Cleaners:</strong> SS-304 upper body with Alumina Ceramic or Polyurethane lower cones.</li></ul><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><ul><li>Operating Consistency: Coarse Screening (2.0%–4.5%), Fine Screening (0.8%–1.5%), LDC Cleaners (0.5%–1.2%)</li><li>System Capacity Range: 30 TPD to 1,000+ TPD</li><li>Screen Basket Perforation Hole Diameters: 1.0 mm to 3.0 mm</li><li>Screen Basket Wedge-Wire Slot Widths: 0.10 mm to 0.35 mm</li><li>Hydrocyclone Operating Pressure: 2.0 bar to 3.5 bar</li><li>Differential Pressure Drop: 0.8 bar to 1.2 bar</li></ul>',
            'key_features_json' => '["Comprehensive High-Density Cleaners, Pressure Screens, and LDC Hydrocyclones", "Non-Blinding Aerofoil Rotors generating suction pulses to maintain continuous slot clearance", "Precision Wedge-Wire Slotted Baskets (down to 0.10 mm) with Hard Chrome Plating", "Low Pressure Drop Design reducing pump energy consumption per ton of pulp", "Alumina Ceramic and Polyurethane Lower Cones for extreme sand and abrasive resistance", "Zero-Fiber-Loss Tailing & Reject Sorters maximizing good fiber recovery", "Full Stainless Steel Vessel Construction polished for corrosion protection and cleanliness"]',
