            'content_html' => '<h1>Crescent Former Tissue Machine</h1><p class="product-description">The Crescent Former Tissue Machine represents state-of-the-art technology for manufacturing high-bulk, ultra-soft tissue paper products. Engineered for speeds up to 1,600 m/min, this machine integrates a hydraulic headbox, crescent forming roll, precision Yankee dryer cylinder, and high-velocity hot air hood to produce facial tissue, toilet paper, and kitchen towels with maximum energy efficiency.</p><h2>System Architecture & Dewatering Dynamics</h2><ul><li><strong>Hydraulic Tissue Headbox:</strong> Single or multi-layer hydraulic headbox with micro-turbulent diffuser tubes engineered to deliver jet velocities up to 1,600 m/min at precise impingement angles into the crescent forming nip.</li><li><strong>Crescent Former Unit:</strong> The pulp slurry is pressed between a forming fabric and a felt over a solid forming roll. Gentle centrifugal dewatering ensures rapid water removal, high fiber retention, and excellent MD/CD tensile strength ratios.</li><li><strong>Yankee Dryer Cylinder:</strong> Large-diameter (12 ft to 18 ft) Cast Iron or Welded Steel Yankee Dryer ground to a mirror finish and operating at steam pressures up to 10 bar. Paired with rigid oscillating creping doctors to generate precise micro-crepe bulk and softness.</li><li><strong>High-Velocity Hot Air Hood:</strong> Direct gas-fired or steam-heated air hood blowing impingement air up to 500°C at high velocities (up to 150 m/s) against the wet web on the Yankee cylinder for rapid drying.</li><li><strong>Tissue Pope Reel:</strong> Surface-driven reel winder with gentle nip control to preserve tissue bulk, crepe density, and reel geometry.</li></ul><h2>Key Features and Benefits</h2><ul><li><strong>Crescent Former Technology:</strong> Superior sheet formation, high bulk, and uniform tensile strength balance across all tissue grades.</li><li><strong>High Design Speeds:</strong> Engineered for continuous production speeds from 600 m/min up to 1,600 m/min with low vibration.</li><li><strong>Precision Yankee Dryer:</strong> Cast iron or high-heat-transfer steel construction with metallized protective coating for uniform surface temperature.</li><li><strong>High-Efficiency Hood & Heat Recovery:</strong> Reclaims hot exhaust gas to preheat process water and combustion air, reducing thermal energy costs by 15–20%.</li><li><strong>Multi-Layer Layering Option:</strong> Dual/Triple channel headbox capability allows soft hardwood fibers on outer surfaces and strong softwood fibers in the inner layer.</li><li><strong>Automatic Creping Doctor Control:</strong> Rigid carbon-fiber doctor beam with continuous oscillation ensures consistent tissue hand-feel and blade life.</li></ul><h2>Applications</h2><ul><li>Premium Facial Tissue paper manufacturing.</li><li>Toilet Tissue & Bathroom Tissue paper rolls.</li><li>High-absorbency Kitchen Towels and Industrial Wiping paper.</li><li>Napkins and Hand Towel tissue products.</li></ul><h2>Materials of Construction</h2><ul><li><strong>Headbox & Former Roll:</strong> Solid SS-316L stainless steel shell with polished internal flow surfaces.</li><li><strong>Yankee Dryer Cylinder:</strong> Alloy Cast Iron or High-Permeability Structural Steel with arc-sprayed Stainless Steel metallized coating.</li><li><strong>Air Hood Structure:</strong> Stainless steel inner casing insulated with high-density mineral wool and stainless heat-exchanger tubes.</li><li><strong>Doctor Assembly:</strong> Carbon fiber / alloy steel doctor beams with SS-316L blade holders.</li></ul><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><ul><li>Daily Production Capacity: 20 TPD to 180 TPD per line</li><li>Design Operating Speed: 600 m/min to 1,600 m/min</li><li>Trimmed Web Width Range: 1,800 mm to 4,200 mm</li><li>Tissue Basis Weight (GSM): 12 GSM to 35 GSM (at headbox / reel)</li><li>Yankee Dryer Diameter: 3,660 mm (12 ft) to 5,486 mm (18 ft)</li><li>Air Hood Impingement Temperature: Up to 