            'content_html' => '<h1>Molded Fiber & Pulp Molding Plant</h1><p class="product-description">Our Automated Molded Fiber & Pulp Molding Plants convert recycled paper (ONP, OCC), sugarcane bagasse, bamboo pulp, and agricultural straw into sustainable, high-value molded pulp products. Designed for automatic forming, in-mold thermoforming drying, robotic handling, and precision trimming, these turnkey lines produce eco-friendly packaging and biodegradable foodware as viable alternatives to single-use plastics.</p><h2>Production Line Configurations & Workflow</h2><ul><li><strong>Precision Thermoforming Tableware Lines:</strong> Fully automatic forming, high-temperature in-mold drying, and hydraulic hot-press calibration. Produces smooth, water-resistant, oil-resistant food containers without manual handling.</li><li><strong>Rotary / Reciprocating Industrial & Egg Tray Lines:</strong> High-capacity multi-face rotary forming drums paired with continuous multi-pass gas or steam drying tunnels for egg trays, fruit packaging, and heavy industrial end-caps.</li></ul><h3>Four-Step Automated Process</h3><ol><li><strong>Stock Preparation:</strong> Raw fibers are pulped, screened, and blended with water/oil repellent additives in computerized dosing tanks.</li><li><strong>Vacuum Forming:</strong> Slurry is drawn onto CNC-machined forming molds using vacuum suction and floating pulp inlet control for uniform wall thickness.</li><li><strong>In-Mold Thermoforming & Hot Pressing:</strong> Hydraulic hot-pressing at 180°C to 220°C dries and cures the wet pulp under high tonnage, yielding smooth, rigid products.</li><li><strong>Edge Trimming & Robotic Stacking:</strong> Automated precision die-trimming removes flash, while 6-axis robotic arms stack finished items onto conveyors.</li></ol><h2>Key Features and Benefits</h2><ul><li><strong>Fully Automatic Cycle:</strong> Single-button operation from slurry vacuum suction to hot pressing, edge trimming, and robotic stacking.</li><