or stable specific edge load (SEL) and energy efficiency.</li><li><strong>Welding-Free Screen Basket Design:</strong> Eliminates heat-affected zone (HAZ) stress points, preventing slot cracking and increasing basket fatigue life.</li><li><strong>Hard Chrome & Carbide Coatings:</strong> 100–200 micron coating thickness protects against severe silica sand, tramp metal, and filler erosion.</li><li><strong>ISO G2.5 Dynamic Rotor Balancing:</strong> Precision dynamic balancing ensures vibration-free rotation, protecting screen drive bearings and seals.</li><li><strong>Extended Service Lifespan:</strong> Increases component operational hours by 30% to 50%, reducing unplanned mill shutdowns and wear part replacement costs.</li><li><strong>Universal Compatibility:</strong> Engineered for direct drop-in replacement across all major international brands of disc refiners and pressure screens.</li></ul><h2>Applications</h2><ul><li>Replacement refiner segment plates for Double Disc Refiners, Twin Disc Refiners, Conical Refiners, and Tri-Disc Refiners.</li><li>Replacement wedge-wire screen baskets and rotors for all major brands of coarse, fine, and headbox pressure screens.</li><li>Rotor and extraction plate replacement for High-Consistency and Low-Consistency pulpers.</li><li>Deflaker rings, agitator impellers, and wear scrapers across pulp stock preparation systems.</li></ul><h2>Materials of Construction</h2><ul><li><strong>Refiner Segment Alloys:</strong> 17-4 PH Stainless Steel, SS-316L, SS-420, and High-Chrome Nickel Alloys (Heat-treated hardness 38–58 HRC).</li><li><strong>Screen Basket Wire & Rings:</strong> SS-316L / SS-316Ti wedge-wire profile with Hard Chrome Plated surface.</li><li><strong>Rotors & Agitator Impellers:</strong> Cast SS-304 / SS-316 with Stellite / Tungsten Carbide hard-faced leading edges.</li></ul><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><ul><li>Refiner Segment Sizes: 13" to 54" diameter (330 mm to 1370 mm)</li><li>Screen Basket Slot Width Range: 0.08 mm to 0.50 mm (slotted)</li><li>Screen Basket Perforation Sizes: 1.0 mm to 4.0 mm (drilled/punched)</li><li>Screen Basket Open Area: 8% to 18%</li><li>Metallurgical Hardness Rating: 35 HRC to 60 HRC (custom heat-treated)</li><li>Dynamic Balance Quality Grade: ISO 1940 Grade G2.5</li></ul>',
